Github Repository for April Loy's fall '24 & Spring '25 independent study

In order to study the racial disparity in local pollution, this code analyzes a large corpus of data from the TEMPO satellite

TEMPO is in geostationary orbit above Turtle Island and Mexico (Mexico city to Northern Canada) and takes once-daily scans of various pollutants

This study is concerned primarily with NO2 and HCHO (formaldehyde) pollution within cities in New York state

This project is in active development, and does not represent a final project. As such, there might be bugs, and certain parts might be under-commented
